{"id": "JAH-SIG-AUTOMATE-000001", "slug": "tool-automated-tool-builder-signature", "title": "Automated Tool Builder \u2014 Overview and definition", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "tool database record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature edition. Original Signature methods and framings developed for the JAH system, labeled Signature throughout. Generates candidate tool implementations from structured requirements. The Automated Tool Builder turns a structured tool specification \u2014 name, inputs, outputs, behavior rules \u2014 into a candidate implementation: generated code, a test suite, and documentation. Every candidate is executed against its tests before delivery, and failures come back with the failing test named. A code-generation method; candidates are starting points, not certified tools. Capability specification and design target: this database describes what the tool must do, not a claim of implementation or deployment. Defensive and engineering content only \u2014 no weapon-targeting or attack-execution content.", "capabilities": ["Spec-to-code generation", "Test-suite generation per tool", "Execute-before-delivery verification", "Failure reporting with test names", "Documentation drafting"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Tool overview and capability inventory", "code": "J({tool:TOOL.name,capabilities:TOOL.capabilities,count:TOOL.capabilities.length});assert(TOOL.capabilities.length>=5,'caps');", "verified_output": "{\"tool\":\"Automated Tool Builder\",\"capabilities\":[\"Spec-to-code generation\",\"Test-suite generation per tool\",\"Execute-before-delivery verification\",\"Failure reporting with test names\",\"Documentation drafting\"],\"count\":5}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "catalog-100-darpa-nasa-grade-tools-2026-10-21.txt", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}